{
  "format": "cogbench-entities/0",
  "source": "player-stats.json, enemies.json and entities-damage.md of the research dir, re-tuned for the 10-frame decision tick (windups are 10 to 20 frames); barrels, bottles and the world wand tiers are ours (cp1-feedback.md section 1, design.md section 3)",
  "notes": [
    "SECRET POTIONS (CP2, 2026-10-27): eight potions exist only as the product of a recipe of three ingredients (materials.json tag secret_potion; cogbench-rules draws the recipes from the rule seed). potion_lively gives regeneration; the other seven give the statuses invulnerable, mana_regen, crit_boost, berserk, levitation, invisible and fireproof. The numbers of all of them are in `statuses` (strength) and `drink` (frames of status per swallowed cell); a full 400-cell bottle gives: regeneration 6.7 s (Noita: Lively Concoction 7.5 s), invulnerable 10 s, mana_regen 20 s (Noita: Concentrated Mana 20 s), crit_boost 15 s, berserk 15 s (Noita: Berserkium 15 s), levitation 10 s, invisible 10 s, fireproof 15 s. A smaller batch lasts proportionally less.",
    "Secret potions work by drinking only (no stain, no contact status). The ordinary potions (heal, mana, haste) are unchanged and are found in the world; a secret potion is never placed in the world.",
    "BOTTLES (2026-10-27, batch D1b): a bottle holds a mixture of materials up to items.bottle.capacity cells in all, like a flask of Noita. Fill adds whatever liquid is scooped; pour, drink and a thrown bottle's spill take the same share of every material. Inside a bottle the secret recipes of the world run (and no other reaction): where all three ingredients of a recipe are present, up to items.bottle.mix_cells_per_frame cells of each turn into that many cells of the potion every frame (3 in, 3 out per triple, like the grid rule recipe_mix; 4 a frame is about a contact line of 16 cells), so a full 400-cell bottle of an equal mixture is done in about 35 frames."
  ],
